  ^
methods.bas:50:1: v is a let: it can't change
  v.scale(2)
  ^
methods.bas:51:11: length takes self: call it on a Vec
  print Vec.length(v); " "; v.polar(1).x; " "; v.nothing(); " "; Vec.nothing(1)
            ^
methods.bas:51:29: polar is called on its type: Vec.polar(..)
  print Vec.length(v); " "; v.polar(1).x; " "; v.nothing(); " "; Vec.nothing(1)
                              ^
methods.bas:51:48: a Vec has no method nothing
  print Vec.length(v); " "; v.polar(1).x; " "; v.nothing(); " "; Vec.nothing(1)
                                                 ^
methods.bas:51:68: a Vec has no method nothing
  print Vec.length(v); " "; v.polar(1).x; " "; v.nothing(); " "; Vec.nothing(1)
                                                                     ^
methods.bas:52:9: a Vec has no method length2
  print v.length2(); " "; v.length
          ^
methods.bas:52:27: length is a method: call it, with (..)
  print v.length2(); " "; v.length
                            ^
